Think: I have a syntax error in my awk command. Let me fix it by using a simpler approach to extract file extensions and create the file types breakdown.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F',' '{
  path = $1;
  size = $2;
  n = split(path, parts, "/");
  filename = parts[n];
  if (match(filename, /\.([^.]+)$/)) {
    ext = substr(filename, RSTART+1, RLENGTH-1);
  } else {
    ext = "no_extension";
  }
  count[ext]++;
  total_size[ext] += size;
} END {
  for (ext in count) {
    print ext ": " count[ext] " files, " total_size[ext] " bytes";
  }
}' temp_workspace/regular_files.csv | sort > temp_workspace/file_types.txt
```

